 [17592186338468 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338468 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338468 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186338137 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338468 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6f92cb71-8832-51de-ba25-618de4d73dc2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338833 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338468 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338833 #edb/ref 1069 "q-70833" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338833 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338833 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,0,-3)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=⟨-3,2,0⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,0,1⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338833 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ee138f11-2a9e-5208-a49a-f5a947f6c08b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338833 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨2,0,-3⟩.$\n\nNow, we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =2i+3j \\\\  & =⟨2,3,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,3,0⟩ & =⟨2,0,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨2,3,0⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,3,0⟩ & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨2,3,0⟩ & =4 \\\\ 2x+3y & =4 \\\\ 2x+3y-4 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419402 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186419424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419402 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/re